From: InterGenJLU <intergenjlu@noreply.intergenos.local>
Subject: [PATCH] image.c: suppress benign EFI-stub kernel warnings on stderr

sbsigntool 0.9.5's PE/COFF parser emits two stderr messages on every
sign of a Linux EFI-stub kernel:

  1. "warning: data remaining[X vs Y]: gaps between PE/COFF sections?"
     fires because the kernel's PE optional header SizeOfImage doesn't
     cover the trailing bzImage payload. sbsigntool correctly adds the
     trailing bytes to its checksum_regions list (as the "endjunk"
     region) so Authenticode signs the entire file. The warning is
     purely informational — the signature is valid.

  2. "Signing Unsigned original image"
     fires on every fresh sign as a positive-confirmation message.
     rc=0 + signed output size are sufficient confirmation for our
     pipeline; the stderr line is noise.

Both fire on every install run via Forge's bare-vmlinuz MOK signing
step (installer/backend/bootloader.py: _install_signed_efi_chain).
2026-05-27 install #28 trace anomaly E.

Patch removes the two `fprintf(stderr, ...)` calls; the underlying
operations (the "endjunk" checksum region, the cert table allocation)
are preserved. No behavior change for signature validity.

--- a/src/image.c
+++ b/src/image.c
@@ -435,9 +435,15 @@
 		r->data = image->buf + bytes;
 		r->size = image->size - bytes - image->cert_table_size;

-		fprintf(stderr, "warning: data remaining[%zd vs %zd]: gaps "
-				"between PE/COFF sections?\n",
-				bytes + image->cert_table_size, image->size);
+		/*
+		 * InterGenOS patch — suppress benign "data remaining"
+		 * warning. Trailing data after declared PE sections is
+		 * normal for Linux EFI-stub kernels (bzImage payload
+		 * after the PE header). The "endjunk" checksum region
+		 * above includes those bytes in the signed range so
+		 * Authenticode is correct; the warning is purely
+		 * informational and fires on every kernel signing.
+		 */
 	} else if (bytes + image->cert_table_size > image->size) {
 		fprintf(stderr, "warning: checksum areas are greater than "
 				"image size. Invalid section table?\n");
@@ -554,7 +560,12 @@
 		start = image->sigbuf + image->sigsize;
 		image->sigsize += aligned_size;
 	} else {
-		fprintf(stderr, "Signing Unsigned original image\n");
+		/*
+		 * InterGenOS patch — suppress purely-informational
+		 * "Signing Unsigned original image" message. sbsign
+		 * emits this on every fresh sign; rc=0 + signed output
+		 * size are sufficient confirmation for our pipeline.
+		 */
 		start = image->sigbuf = talloc_array(image, uint8_t, aligned_size);
 		image->sigsize = aligned_size;
 	}
